 ### Scalability
+- `./zn skills --check` reads two folders, starts one `readlink` per `.claude/skills` entry (12 today) and runs one `git ls-files -s`: 0.5 s in the gate's static stage, beside the 1.1 s format stage, so it adds no wall time.
+- `lessons.load` does what it did, over two folders instead of one.
+- `renderPrompt` adds one registry load and one skills load per prompt.
+
 ### Maintainability
+- The next skill is a folder plus `./zn skills`, with no code change; the next project's skills are `<name>/skills/<name>-…`.
+- One reader of skill folders (`skills.luau`), used by the command, the gate, the prompt and the lessons.
+- The names live in one table (§1), and the rename script holds the same mapping for ids.
+
 ### Usability
+- The names say the step: `z-` is the pipeline in order (`z-ticket` … `z-stop`), and `zz-` is what a step calls.
+- `/z-run R0010` replaces `/launch-raft R0010`, and the board copies it.
+- Every refusal of `./zn skills` names the folder or link and what to do.
+- `z-nile/README.md` is one page with the picture first.
 
